<title>NEW ZEALAND: Air NZ sees more investment, alliances.</title>
<headline>Air NZ sees more investment, alliances.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Air New Zealand Chief Executive Jim McCrea said on Thursday that at current forecast rates of growth, the national flag carrier would need NZ$240 million a year to replace existing aircraft.</p>
<p>&quot;At current forecast rates of growth we will be committing investments of more than NZ$240 million a year to replace existing aircraft and secure carrying capacity, or we must achieve an equivalent result though alliance strategies,&quot; McCrea told an Auckland business conference.</p>
<p>-- Wellington Newsroom (64-4-4734746)</p>
</text>
